## Safety posture

A default scaffold is **read-only**. It prints this at startup, and it is the
one thing in this project you can rely on:

```
Web3 mode: READ-ONLY
Signing: DISABLED
Broadcasting: DISABLED
Custody: NONE
Private keys: NOT GENERATED
```

If the two consent-gated modules are present, two of those lines change to
`CONSENT-GATED MODULE PRESENT`, and the application prints a warning that
broadcasting is still never called automatically. That warning is not
decoration: the broadcasting module requires a human confirmation callback that
must return exactly `true`, on every single call, and it has no scheduler.

Guarantees, in full:

| Guarantee | Where it comes from |
|---|---|
| No private key is generated, requested, imported, derived or stored | Nothing in the codebase calls a key-management API. See `SECURITY.md`. |
| Nothing is signed by default | `src/wallet/signing.ts` is not written to disk without the consent flag. |
| Nothing is broadcast by default | `src/wallet/broadcast.ts` is not written to disk without the consent flag. |
| Nothing is ever broadcast automatically | Even with both modules present, every send needs a human confirmation returning exactly `true`. |
| The default chain is a testnet | `assertDefaultChainIsTestnet()` runs at import. Mainnet is not configured at all. |
| No RPC URL or credential is bundled | `RPC_URL` is empty in `.env.example`, and `config.ts` refuses to guess an endpoint. |
| No scheduled or autonomous on-chain action | There is no timer, cron, queue or retry loop anywhere in the project. |

